              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
        Notice that <fr:link href="/sub-0006/" title="the core of adjoint monotone functions › https://hejohns.github.io/sub-0006/" uri="https://hejohns.github.io/sub-0006/" display-uri="sub-0006" type="local">the above proof</fr:link> does <html:em>not</html:em> use the information that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u]]></fr:tex> is monotone.
        Thus <fr:link href="/hejohns-0006/" title="the core of adjoint monotone functions" uri="https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns-0006/" display-uri="hejohns-0006" type="local">the above lemma</fr:link> holds where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u]]></fr:tex> are just a priori functions.
        The <fr:link href="/hejohns-0006/" title="the core of adjoint monotone functions" uri="https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns-0006/" display-uri="hejohns-0006" type="local">above lemma</fr:link> is in some sense the more
        immediately natural question, but can be easily strengthened to
        the form of this corollary.
    </html:p>
